            <div xml:id="d115">

                <pb facs="0292" n="158" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg158"/>

                <head>No. 115.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hosmer to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States in Central America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1888-06-21"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi>
                            21, 1888</date>. (Received July 9.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 823.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 818, of the 9th
                    instant, in which I inclosed to you a copy of my note to the minister for
                    foreign affairs of Guatemala, imparting to him your views in respect to the
                    provision of peace and friendship in the annulled treaty of 1849, I now have the
                    honor to inclose to you a translated copy of Minister Barrutia’s reply to my
                    note, received by me June 13, although bearing date on the 9th instant, in which
                    lie concurs in the views I expressed in accordance with your instructions.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James R. Hosmer</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad
                        interim.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d115-a1.xml" xpointer="d115-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
